Our per-dataset NL baseline is competitive with Span-ASTE across all four datasets and matches or exceeds GTS. It falls 3--4 points below BTF-CCL and MvP, both of which use specialised techniques (cross-granularity contrastive learning and 10-dataset multi-task training respectively). This confirms that our model is a reasonable representative of the generative ABSA approach --- not state-of-the-art in-domain, but solidly in the competitive range.

\subsection{Out-of-Domain Comparison}

Having established that our model performs credibly in-domain, we now compare all method families in the OOD setting --- the primary focus of this thesis. Table~\ref{tab:crossmethod} shows results when training on Rest14 and testing on Laptop14.

\begin{table}[htbp]
